# Fableland — Zone 6 and the Rules of a Place GDD

Zone 6 (第六区) is not a recoloured copy of the outer five. It is a stage of its own, with its
own mechanic and its own story, and it **rotates**: each run is one of several variants. This
document defines the first two — **The Void Frontier (虚无边境)** and **Avīci (无间地狱)** — the
twelve bosses they field, and the system both are built on: **the rules of a place**, which
also carries each outer realm's own **law** (Wulin's is the first).

First landed in **v0.12.0** (design + engine, stand-in kits). Every number below is
**provisional** — recorded in the Decisions log (§10) — except the owner's own: the Void
Frontier's −20 % / +10 % gravity steps and Wulin's "one more jump, each 0.75 as high".

Code: `Scripts/Data/Zone6Table.cs`, `Scripts/Data/RealmLawTable.cs`, `Scripts/Data/BossTable.cs`
(the twelve rows), `Scripts/Run/Zone6State.cs`, `Scripts/Run/ArenaRules.cs`,
`Scripts/Orchestration/Arena/ArenaRulesApplier.cs`, `Scripts/Hazard/StyxTideHazard.cs`.
Check: `Scenes/Run/Zone6Check.tscn`, and the zone-6 walk of `Scenes/Run/RunWalkCheck.tscn`.

---

## 1. The owner's brief

> 我们的第六区其实并不是前五个区的简单换色，而是有自己的机制和故事线。我们先做两个进行轮换
> 探索一下美术风格。计划中 每一种第六区都对应一种独特的机制 可能是debuff 可能是地图风格
> 可能是 接触方式 等等。… 普通的realms也可能有不同的features 是独属于这个realms本身的。…
> 武林世界 所有角色可以多跳一次 但是每次跳跃高度只有正常的0.75倍。… 虚无边境 … 穿越冥河后
> 达到的生与死的交界。在这里，每打败一个boss重力就会减少20%，失败则会增加10%，直到最终进入
> 虚空迎接最后的挑战 … 最终的boss地图将会非常空旷 所以如果受到重力太多可能很难躲避。…
> 无间地狱的小boss是五毒 贪嗔痴慢疑 … 黑暗佛教风格。每打过一个boss，最终boss就会被封印一种
> 能力，但是被打败自己却会被封印一种能力（… 无法被清除的debuff …）

What that asks for, and where it lands:

| Ask | Here |
|-----|------|
| Zone 6 has its own mechanic and story; two variants rotate | §3, §4, §5 |
| Each variant: a unique mechanic — a debuff, a map style, a way of touching | Void Frontier: gravity. Avīci: seals |
| Realms can have features of their own; Wulin: +1 jump, 0.75 height | §2, `MapGDD.md` §2.3 |
| Void Frontier: −20 % gravity per win, +10 % per loss; an empty final map | §4 |
| Avīci: the five poisons; a dark Buddhist final boss; win → he loses a power, lose → you gain an uncleansable debuff | §5 |
| "Think about the rest" — the five guardians, both final bosses | §4.1, §4.2, §5.2 |

---

## 2. The rules of a place

A fight's **rules** are what the place it happens in does to the bodies in it: the realm's law,
zone 6's variant, the seals a run carries. One record (`ArenaRules`) holds them; the run
computes it when a node is entered and hands it to the arena with the rest of the handshake
(`AdventureContext.Rules`, T10 §3). The arena puts it on **every body that enters it** — the
opening fighter, a switch-in, a boss staged after the countdown, a wave of adds — as
source-keyed modifiers (golden rule 7). A projectile takes its thrower's share of gravity when
it is thrown. **A kit never reads the map or the run** (T00): it only finds itself lighter,
jumping again, slower to reload.

**Realm laws** (`MapGDD.md` §2.3 is their home): one data row per world (`RealmLawTable`),
applied with source `realm:<code>` to every fighter on both sides — protagonists and a
Foe-side boss alike — and to ordinary foes only when the row says so (then its gravity only).
Shown as one line at the start of every fight in that realm, and listed on the HUD for the
whole fight.

| World | Realm | Law | Rule | Foes? |
|-------|-------|-----|------|-------|
| BM | Wulin (武林) | **Qinggong (轻功)** | +1 jump on top of each kit's own; every jump 0.75 as high (launch ×√0.75). Ground jumps, air jumps and swim strokes alike; coyote time and the jump cooldown unchanged | no |
| the other seven | — | TBD #62 | — | — |

Measured (Zone6Check): Pomegraknight rises **8.3 m** on her one jump; under Qinggong **6.2 m**
on each of two (×0.75).

**Zone 6 never applies the law of the world whose map it borrows.** It has rules of its own.

**Who takes what.**

| Rule | Fighters (Player side) | Fighters (Foe side: a boss) | Ordinary foes | Projectiles |
|------|------|------|------|------|
| A realm's law | yes | yes | only if the row says so, gravity only | — |
| The Void Frontier's gravity | yes | yes | yes | the thrower's share, at the throw |
| Avīci's seals | yes — every protagonist | no | no | — |
| Māra's sealed powers | — | the final boss only | — | — |

---

## 3. Zone 6 as a stage

**The variant.** Chosen once per run, from the seed, on a stream of its own
(`seed:zone6:variant`): no number any other system draws moves, so every existing seed still
generates the same world, and a save from before v0.12.0 — which stores no variant — is given
its seed's. Across 400 seeds the two are dealt 185 / 215. A debug knob (§8) forces one.
*Rotation as meta-progression — which variants a player meets, unlocks — is TBD #63.*

**Five gates and the core.** The geography is the generator's, untouched (`MapGDD.md` §7):

| Node | Is | Foe level | Timer | Losing it |
|------|----|-----------|-------|-----------|
| `XX-5-1` … `XX-5-5` | the variant's five **mini-bosses**, one per node in order (`MiniBossIds[0..4]`) | 7 | 240 s | **survived** (below) |
| `XX-R` | the river hub | — | — | — |
| `XX-6-1` | the variant's **final boss** | 8 | 360 s | **the run ends** (TwistedReality aside) |

The mission the generator rolled into an LV5 node stays in the graph; the handshake overrides
it (`Mission = Boss`, `BossId` = that gate's warden). No draw moves. Mini-bosses scale by the
node's foe level exactly as a realm's boss scales by the day's (`FOES.gdd` §8.2).

**A mini-boss defeat does not end the run.** A defeat is the fighter in play falling (the arena
never sends a benched fighter in on a death — `NODES.gdd` §2.2) or the gate's timer running
out. Then:
- every member of the battle team comes back with **at least 25 % HP** (`DefeatHpFloor`);
- the node stays **unconquered**, and the player is sent back to where they came from;
- the variant's **penalty** applies (§4, §5), and a toast says what it was;
- the day must still be finished; the gate can be fought again, with no limit.

The **first** victory at a gate pays the variant's **reward**; a gate already conquered pays
nothing more. A zone-6 boss recruits nobody and gives no item: the reward *is* the variant's.

**Maps.** A gate is fought on the map it was always dealt (`MapGDD.md` §7): a map of one of
the run's five worlds **for the mission the generator rolled into it**, drawn VOID-touched in
the variant's look (§6); the mini-boss perches on its Level Goal markers. So no map moves and
none is orphaned. A variant may give its final boss a **fixed arena** (`FinalArenaMapId`):
the Void Frontier does; Avīci's core is dealt a run world's boss arena, as before.

---

## 4. The Void Frontier (虚无边境)

*Past the River Styx, the shore where life and death touch.* The far bank is where every
storybook's dead wash up — and every afterlife sends its ferrymen and judges. Each guardian you
beat loosens the living world's hold: you grow **lighter**. Lose, and you fall back heavier with
life. At the end the shore gives out into the Void, where something that was never written
waits — on a floor with nothing to hide behind but the air.

**Gravity, G.** 1.0 on arrival. **×0.8 per mini-boss victory, ×1.1 per defeat** (the owner's
numbers), clamped to **[0.25, 2.0]**. G is on every fighter on both sides, every foe, and every
gravity projectile (a seed, a head, a gull's dropping takes its thrower's G when thrown). **The
launch speed is unchanged** — so a jump at G = 0.5 goes twice as high and hangs twice as long.
Five clean wins: ×0.328. A loss first, then five wins: ×0.360.

### 4.1 The five guardians (mini-bosses)

Authoritative look and skills. Every guardian is drawn as a cyanotype photogram with **one spot
colour** of its own (§7). Until its kit is built each fields the stand-in (§9).

| Node | Guardian | Spot | Look | Skills |
|------|----------|------|------|--------|
| XX-5-1 | **The Ferryman (渡魂人)** | amber | a hooded giant in a skiff, an amber lantern, an oar, a string of obols | **Oar Sweep** (BA), **Obol Toss**, **Undertow**, **Skiff Ram** |
| XX-5-2 | **The Weigher of Hearts (称心官)** | gold | a jackal-headed judge, a gold collar, a balance | **Feather Fan**, **Judgement** — the arena's two scale pans are platforms that tilt; the low pan sinks into a hazard — **Devourer's Jaws** |
| XX-5-3 | **Meng Po of the Naihe Bridge (孟婆)** | red | a small old woman, an iron ladle, a cauldron, a red lantern, bowls | **Soup Lob** — *Forget*: your next skill press within 4 s fails — **Ladle Sweep**, **Bridge Mist**; her arena is one long bridge |
| XX-5-4 | **Xolotl, the Soul-Dog of Mictlan (冥犬修洛特)** | jade | a skeletal dog-god on backward feet, a jade collar, lightning | **Pounce**, **Carry** (drags you 1.5 s), **Lightning Howl** |
| XX-5-5 | **Stingy Jack, the Lantern Wanderer (守灯杰克)** | ember orange | a lanky wanderer, an ember in a carved turnip | **Ember Toss** (sets OnFire), **Lantern Step**, **Lights Out** (3 s of dark) |

**The Ferryman in numbers** (first-pass; **his own kit since v0.12.1** — `Scripts/Bosses/Zone6/Ferryman.cs`):

| Skill | What it does |
|-------|--------------|
| Oar Sweep (BA) | a cone 5 m deep, ±50°: 30 damage and an 18 m/s horizontal shove; every 1.4 s |
| Obol Toss (S1, 6 s) | a fan of 3 coins lobbed at 45°, the middle one thrown to land on the player under the gravity he — and so his coins — feels (G included), one short, one long: 10 damage and **−150 ult charge** each — the toll, net of the charge the blow itself pays the victim |
| Undertow (S2, 12 s) | every fighter within 14 m is dragged toward him at 4 m/s for 2.5 s; then he sweeps |
| Skiff Ram (below 50 % HP, every 15 s) | a 0.8 s lantern telegraph, then he rides across at 16 m/s: 40 damage and a knock-up |
| Brain | Undertow when you are beyond 8 m (and within its 14 m) and it is ready; Sweep within 5 m; Obol at 5–14 m; Ram in phase 2 when ready; otherwise hold near the river's edge — the perch he opened on, on foot |

Measured (BossFightCheck §5): the Undertow drags a still player **8.0 m in 2 s** and ends in a
sweep that lands; an obol takes **150** ult charge from a player 8 m away; the Ram holds still
through its telegraph, rides at **16.0 m/s** and throws the player up at **21.5 m/s**.

### 4.2 The Unwritten (无名者) — the final boss

*A faceless figure of torn pages and erased ink, with a hole for a face: the one character no
storybook ever wrote, who tore the books apart looking for a story of its own.* Proposed as the
run's **dark leader** (TBD #1).

| Skill | What it does |
|-------|--------------|
| **Styx Tide** (signature) | the river at the horizon rears up and **sweeps the whole floor from one side**: jump it, or it hits hard (30 % of max HP) and **carries** you with it |
| **Rising Tide** | below half HP, two waves in succession (1.1 s apart); below a quarter, the second comes from the other side |
| **Borrowed Shapes** | a phase in which it fights with the kit of one of your own party |
| **Blank Page** | a white-out: the screen goes blank but for the fighters |

**The Styx Tide punishes high gravity.** A wall of water 5.5 m tall and 3 m deep at 14 m/s.
Only up escapes it — a slab above it is as safe as the air — so how long a jump hangs is
everything. Measured with real bodies (Zone6Check §5: Pomegraknight, one jump, lanes jumping at
every other tick):

| Gravity | Window in which one jump clears it | Target |
|---------|-----------------------------------|--------|
| ×0.5 | **1.33 s** | comfortable at ≤ ×0.6 |
| ×1.0 | **0.30 s** | clearable only with good timing |
| ×1.5 | **0** | nearly impossible from ×1.3 (one jump cannot; a double-jump kit can) |

Arithmetic (for tuning): a jump launched at 32 m/s stays above 5.5 m for
2·√(32² − 2·64G·5.5) / (64G) s; the wave takes (3 + 1.5) m / 14 m/s ≈ 0.32 s to pass a body.
At G ≈ 1.25 the two meet. Schedule: the first wave 6 s after the boss is staged, one every 9 s,
its side drawn from a stream of its own (`arena:<node>:mission:styx`).

**Its arena.** *An empty floor; the Styx at the horizon; the only escape is up.* Until it is
painted (Z6-VF-F, §7), the core is fought on **`starfield_sea_level_sl`**: Starland's
sea-level plain — one unbroken floor and three slabs, drawn VOID-touched in the Void Frontier's
look. (Not Starland's boss arena: its 12 m plateau would stand above the tide all fight.)

*Implemented in v0.12.0:* the Styx Tide and the Rising Tide, on the stand-in kit.
*Deferred:* Borrowed Shapes, Blank Page, its own kit.

---

## 5. Avīci (无间地狱)

*The lowest hell, without interval.* Māra, lord of desire and death, keeps the five poisons at
its gates. Beat a poison and Māra loses the power it fed; lose to one and it **enters you** — a
seal that nothing can cleanse.

### 5.1 The five poisons (mini-bosses)

Each stack of a seal applies to **every protagonist** of the run, for the rest of the run, in
every fight; a further defeat by the same poison adds a stack, **up to 3**. Seals cannot be
cleansed — no blessing, heal, shelter or item removes them (`Zone6State` exposes no way to;
Zone6Check proves a blessing and a heal leave them). They show on the HUD in every fight and on
the map.

| Node | Poison | Warden | Seal, per stack | Māra loses |
|------|--------|--------|-----------------|------------|
| XX-5-1 | 贪 Greed | **Preta, the Hungry Ghost (饿鬼)** — grey-green, a huge belly, a needle throat. **Gorge** (inhales; swallowed projectiles heal it), **Spew**, **Hungry Grasp** | **Hunger**: reload time +30 % | **Devour** — heals from the damage he deals |
| XX-5-2 | 嗔 Anger | **Asura of Wrath (修罗)** — three faces, six arms, a tiger skin, a flame aureole. **Six-Arm Flurry**, **Wrath Fire**, **Vajra Throw**, **Rising Wrath** | **Smoulder**: damage taken +15 % | **Wrath** — an enraged phase below half HP |
| XX-5-3 | 痴 Delusion | **The Boar of Delusion (痴猪)** — a black boar with closed eyes. **Blind Charge** (stuns itself on a wall), **Mirror Herd**, **Mire** (left and right swap) | **Fog**: skill cooldowns +25 % | **Delusion** — mirror images |
| XX-5-4 | 慢 Pride | **The Fallen Deva (衰天)** — a god in the five decays. **Heavy Halo**, **Wilting Garland**, **Pride's Armour** (poise, and a phase taking 70 % less damage) | **Burden**: move speed −15 % | **Iron Throne** — an invulnerable throne phase |
| XX-5-5 | 疑 Doubt | **Ox-Head and Horse-Face (牛头马面)** — two wardens. **Two Minds** (only the real one takes damage; they swap), **Chain Hook**, **Trident Feint** | **Hesitation**: attack interval +20 % | **Doubt** — a curse that makes some of your casts fizzle |

How a seal reaches a body: reload and attack interval through the magazine's multipliers,
damage taken through the defense pool (the defense that makes 100/(100+d) the scale: one stack
of Smoulder is −13.0), cooldowns through the kits' one cooldown helper, move speed on walking,
running and swimming. Measured on all five kits of the roster (Zone6Check §4c): every one takes
×1.15 damage and walks ×0.85 as fast under one stack of each.

**The Asura of Wrath in numbers** (first-pass; **its own kit since v0.12.1** — `Scripts/Bosses/Zone6/AsuraWrath.cs`):

| Skill | What it does |
|-------|--------------|
| Six-Arm Flurry (BA) | 3 cone hits 0.12 s apart, 3.5 m reach, 12 damage each; 4 hits when enraged |
| Wrath Fire (S1, 8 s) | two floor waves, left and right, at 10 m/s for 12 m: 15 damage + 20 OnFire stacks; jumpable |
| Vajra Throw (S2, 7 s) | flies 12 m and returns: 20 damage each way, a small shove |
| Rising Wrath (passive) | attack interval and cooldowns × (1 − 0.4 × the share of HP missing); **enraged** below 50 % HP (cue `passive.wrath.enrage`) |
| Brain | Flurry within 3.5 m; Vajra at 5–12 m; Wrath Fire when you are grounded within 12 m; otherwise close in |

Measured (BossFightCheck §5): Rising Wrath ×0.80 at 51 % HP and ×0.70 at 25 %, on cooldowns
and the attack interval alike; enraged once, below half — the flurry goes from 3 arms to 4; the
vajra strikes a player 4 m away once going and once coming back. (Past about 4.8 m the two
blows land within the player's 0.8 s of post-hit grace, and only the first counts — the return
is for a player who dodged the throw.)

### 5.2 Māra Pāpīyas (天魔波旬) — the final boss

*A black-blue wrathful demon with a crown of five skulls, holding the Wheel of Life in his
claws.* His five powers are the five above; each gate you win **seals** one. Until his kit is
built (the five powers are its design), the stand-in loses **12 % of its HP and 10 points of
damage per sealed power** (`MaraHpPerSeal`, `MaraDamagePerSeal`), applied after his row — at
foe level 8 with two sealed: 3420 of 4500 HP, damage ×1.60 of ×1.80. Five sealed leaves 40 %.

---

## 6. What the player sees and hears

- **The HUD** lists the place's rules under the HP bar for the whole fight — the realm's law;
  `The Void Frontier (虚无边境) · gravity ×0.80`; `Sealed in you: Hunger ×1, Burden ×2`;
  `Sealed in Māra: Wrath, Doubt` — and says the first as a toast when the fight opens. After a
  zone-6 result the toast says what changed ("gravity ×0.88 (was ×1.10)", "贪 Greed enters you —
  sealed with Hunger ×1"), and the list gains where zone 6 now stands.
- **The map's info panel** shows zone 6's status line once the run has crossed into it or
  carries a seal.
- **The look.** A gate's borrowed map is drawn VOID-touched in its variant's look
  (`Zone6Look`: grey = luma(c); out = mix(grey, c, colour kept) × shade + lift):

  | Variant | Colour kept | Shade | Lift | Reads as |
  |---------|-------------|-------|------|----------|
  | (none — before v0.12.0) | 0.22 | 0.50 0.44 0.62 | 0 | drained, darkened toward violet |
  | The Void Frontier | 0.14 | 0.56 0.68 0.70 | 0.10 0.14 0.15 | a cold grey-teal mist |
  | Avīci | 0.24 | 0.66 0.22 0.16 | 0 | dark; what colour is left is fire |

  Fighters, foes, hazards, telegraphs and the HUD keep their colour.
- **Cues.** `flow`/`arena.enter` in zone 6 is tagged with the **variant** (`void_frontier`,
  `avici`), and its magnitude is the backdrop's lightness **after** the treatment — so effects
  are drawn, and the hit flash chooses dark or light, for the canvas actually on screen. The
  VFX director and the music both map the two tags to the **VOID** medium (`VfxTable.Looks`,
  `MusicProfiles.ForArena`). This closes the zone-6 half of TBD #49. The Styx Tide's hit is
  `hazard`/`styx_tide` (a splash in the arena's medium, like the tsunami).

