## 7. Art direction — confirmed by the concept images (2026-11-27)

The images are in `Docs/Art/StyleExploration/zone6/img/` (previews; the full-size PNGs are in
the git-ignored `_originals/`); `manifest.json` beside them holds every prompt in full and
where each came from (Tripo Studio, GPT Image 2.5). Ids below are the manifest's.

### 7.1 The Void Frontier — **cyanotype (蓝晒)**

Prussian-blue ground; the figures white and pale-cyan **photogram silhouettes**, as if objects
had been laid on sensitised paper in the sun; a sun-bleached, brushed sensitiser edge; **no
outlines**. **One spot colour per guardian** — Ferryman amber, Weigher gold, Meng Po red,
Xolotl jade, Jack ember orange — the only warm thing on the page. The concepts hold it well.

| Id | What |
|----|------|
| `Z6-VF-A` | the far shore of the Styx — **cyanotype** (chosen) |
| `Z6-VF-B` | the same shore — Greek black-figure pottery (explored) |
| `Z6-VF-C` | the same shore — hand-tinted magic-lantern slide (explored) |
| `Z6-VF-F` | the final arena: an endless empty floor, the Styx rearing at the horizon into the wave |
| `Z6-VF-1` … `-6` | the Ferryman, the Weigher, Meng Po, Xolotl, Stingy Jack, the Unwritten |
| `Z6-SPR-FERRYMAN` | the source of the in-game sprite |

Prompt core (the arena sheets): *"Side-view 2D platform-fighter arena … the far shore of the
River Styx, where life and death touch — a grey shingle bank, a narrow ferryman's skiff moored
at a crooked jetty with a lantern on its prow, drowned stone stairs …"* + the medium line;
the boss sheets: *"Character concept art of a boss for a 2D side-view action game: <who> …
Full body in a three-quarter view, centred …"*.

### 7.2 Avīci — **Tibetan nagtang (黑唐卡)**

Gold and vermilion line on **black**; flame aureoles; mineral blue and green; the iconography
of the wrathful protectors; **the Wheel of Life held by Māra**. This is the owner's Tibetan
request, and the arena and boss sheets read strongly.

| Id | What |
|----|------|
| `Z6-AV-A` | the gates of Avīci — **nagtang** (chosen) |
| `Z6-AV-B` | the same gates — a Japanese hell scroll (地狱草纸) (explored) |
| `Z6-AV-C` | the same gates — black lacquer with gold leaf (explored) |
| `Z6-AV-F` | Māra's arena: black stone over a sea of fire, Māra colossal behind it |
| `Z6-AV-1` … `-6` | Preta, the Asura, the Boar, the Fallen Deva, Ox-Head and Horse-Face, Māra |
| `Z6-SPR-ASURA` | the source of the in-game sprite |

### 7.3 In-game sprites

Keyed to transparency, 384 px tall, side view facing **left**, no pink fringe:
`Assets/Sprites/Bosses/Ferryman/ferryman.png` (384 × 384, with the oar) and
`Assets/Sprites/Bosses/AsuraWrath/asura_wrath.png` (364 × 384, six arms, the aureole). Scaled
so each boss stands **3.5–4 m** (32 px/m). Used from v0.12.1.

**Not yet decided:** a cyanotype or nagtang *tile kit* for the arenas (each variant's own maps —
TBD #33 continues); whether the VOID treatment's looks (§6) should move toward these media
(a Prussian-blue cast for the Frontier; black-and-gold for Avīci) once maps exist.

