## 10. Decisions log

Every entry is **provisional** — a first pass to be played and confirmed by the owner.

| Date | Decision | Why |
|------|----------|-----|
| 2026-11-27 | The variant is drawn from the seed on a stream of its own (`seed:zone6:variant`); a debug knob and `FABLELAND_ZONE6` force it | Nothing existing moves; a save keeps its seed, so its variant is derivable |
| 2026-11-27 | The five LV5 nodes are the variant's five mini-bosses in node order; the handshake overrides the rolled mission (no draw) | Deterministic mapping; the graph and its signature unchanged |
| 2026-11-27 | A gate keeps the map its rolled mission deals (not a boss arena) | Every map zone 6 dealt stays dealt — `vk_seashore_5` is reachable only there; boss arenas are the core's |
| 2026-11-27 | A mini-boss defeat = the fighter in play falls, or the timer runs out; the team returns with ≥ 25 % HP, the node stays unconquered, the penalty applies, back to the map; no limit on retries | The owner's ladder needs defeats the run survives; 25 % keeps a retry possible |
| 2026-11-27 | Only a gate's **first** win pays the reward; a zone-6 boss recruits nobody and pays no item | The ladder is the reward; no farming a gate |
| 2026-11-27 | The core keeps permadeath (TwistedReality still rewinds it) | The final fight stays final |
| 2026-11-27 | Gravity clamped to [0.25, 2.0] | Multiplicative steps never reach 0 but a losing streak grows without end |
| 2026-11-27 | G applies to fighters on both sides, foes and gravity projectiles; launch speed unchanged | The owner's "gravity" is the world's, not the player's |
| 2026-11-27 | Void Frontier guardians: the Ferryman, the Weigher of Hearts, Meng Po, Xolotl, Stingy Jack — five afterlives' border-keepers, one per run world's culture | "The boundary between life and death" — every storybook's dead come here |
| 2026-11-27 | The Unwritten as the Frontier's final boss, proposed as the dark leader (TBD #1) | A story-eating black hole's last being is one never written |
| 2026-11-27 | Styx Tide: 5.5 m × 3 m at 14 m/s, 30 % max HP and a carry; first at 6 s, every 9 s; Rising Tide below 50 % / both sides below 25 % | Measured: ×0.5 → 1.33 s, ×1 → 0.30 s, ×1.5 → 0 — the targets |
| 2026-11-27 | The Frontier's core on `starfield_sea_level_sl` until its own arena exists | The emptiest shipped flat floor; Starland's boss arena has a 12 m plateau the tide cannot reach |
| 2026-11-27 | Avīci: seals stack to 3; Hunger +30 % reload, Smoulder +15 % damage taken, Fog +25 % cooldowns, Burden −15 % move, Hesitation +20 % attack interval | Each fits its poison; cap 3 keeps Burden from stopping a fighter |
| 2026-11-27 | Māra Pāpīyas as Avīci's final boss; his five powers are the poisons'; the stand-in loses 12 % HP / 10 damage per seal | The owner's "dark Buddhist" lord; the seal must be felt before his kit exists |
| 2026-11-27 | Damage taken goes through the defense pool (additive with other defense); attack interval through the magazine's multiplier | One pool per stat (golden rule 7) |
| 2026-11-27 | A realm's law reaches ordinary foes only if its row says so; Qinggong does not | Crabs with an extra jump would change the foe design |
| 2026-11-27 | Zone 6 never applies a borrowed world's law | It has rules of its own |
| 2026-11-27 | Per-variant VOID looks (grey-teal mist; fire on black); `arena.enter` tagged with the variant at the drained lightness | Closes TBD #49's zone-6 half |
| 2026-11-27 | Art: the Void Frontier in **cyanotype** with one spot colour per guardian; Avīci in **Tibetan nagtang**. Explored and kept on file: black-figure pottery, magic-lantern slide; hell scroll, black lacquer and gold | Confirmed by the concept images (§7) |
| 2026-11-27 | v0.12.1: a zone-6 kit is a Foe-side fighter that is nobody's protagonist (`Zone6BossFighter`), its row's damage share and bulk kept (× the node's level), one static sprite mirrored by its scene so the body's facing flips it | The same rules as every boss; no animation yet |
| 2026-11-27 | The obols are aimed by range (45°, v = √(d·g·G)), not thrown at a fixed speed | Under this game's gravity (64 m/s²) a fixed 13 m/s throw lands 2 m away; aimed, the fan brackets the player at any range and any G |
| 2026-11-27 | The obol's toll is net of the ult charge its own blow pays the victim | Otherwise a 150 toll reads 138 |
| 2026-11-27 | The Ferryman holds his perch on foot (no jumping); the Ram rides level along the floor he stands on | First pass; a skiff that leaves the floor is for his own arena |

